''Version:'' 0.1.4-beta.1 · ''Status:'' Experimental

Convert MuseScore and MusicXML files into editable ABC with an actual sheet-music preview. Supports batch import and passes the results to TiddlyWiki's standard pending `$:/Import` tiddler for final confirmation.

!! Workflow

# Select one or more `.mscz`, `.mscx`, `.musicxml`, `.xml`, or `.mxl` files.
# Select the staves, voices, measure range, and ''full'' measures per line (default 4).
# Review the rendered score and conversion warnings. Optionally edit the ABC source.
# Click ''Send to TiddlyWiki import''. Then use the native `$:/Import` dialog to select, deselect, rename, and import the resulting tiddlers.

!! Beams, repeats and pickup measures

* Explicit beam groups are retained from MuseScore/MusicXML when possible. If the source contains no explicit beams, cautious beat-based grouping is inferred. Always compare with the source score.
* Adjacent end-repeat `:|` and start-repeat `|:` are combined into one `::` boundary without an empty measure.
* With four full measures per line, a short pickup measure can yield five physical measures on that line. This also covers an isolated 2/4 measure inside a prevailing 4/4 passage. Genuine 7/8 ↔ 9/8 meter changes count normally.
* The ABCJS preview respects the source line breaks instead of overwriting them with automatic wrapping.

!! Instrument names and page fit

* The importer no longer appends synthetic labels such as `system 1` or `system 2` to the `V:` header. The score prints only a concise instrument name.
* Long source names use the MuseScore/MusicXML short form where available, otherwise a short display label. Original names are preserved in `huwiki-import-original-instruments`.
* Multiple staves belonging to one MuseScore part get a printed label only on the first selected stave. Internal voice IDs remain unchanged.
* Previously imported ABC tiddlers are not changed automatically. Re-import the original file or edit the `V:` header names manually.
* Dense scores can still require fewer full measures per line (e.g., 2–3) in the importer.

!! Compatibility and limitations

* MuseScore MSCZ/MSCX and MusicXML/MXL; max 20 files per batch.
* Output ABC tiddlers use `abc-source`, `abc-bars-per-line`, and `ABC`/`Musik` tags. Conversion runs locally and works offline with embedded ABCJS/JSZip.
* Independent of the existing Music Edition ABC plugin.
* Not lossless: check tuplets, ornaments, voices, transposition, compound meters, endings, and beaming.

!! Authors and licenses

* HUWiki contributors (AI-assisted development), MIT, © 2026.
* ABCJS 6.7.2: MIT; Petaluma font: SIL OFL 1.1.
* JSZip 3.10.1: MIT.
* See the ''license'' tab for full third-party license text.
